\section{Introduction}
Kadung (ISO 639-3 dkg; Glottocode vagh1248) is a Plateau (Benue-Congo) language of Plateau and Bauchi states, Nigeria. Sources treat it as part of a small dialect cluster with Ya and Bijim (Kwanka); mutual intelligibility with them is reported to be fairly low. Speaker estimates range from about 19,000 to 21,000. Very little educational material was found in search; this report lists only what appeared in search results.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes for Kadung were found in search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Kwanka language (dialect cluster including Kadung, Ya, Bijim): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kwanka_language}
\item ASJP word list for Kadung: \url{https://asjp.clld.org/languages/KADUNG}
\item Glottolog entry for Vaghat/Kadung: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/vagh1248.bigmap.html}
